
  {%- comment -%} Hidden product form shared by every "Add to cart" button on this page {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- form 'product', product, id: form_id, data-type: 'add-to-cart-form', is: 'product-form', class: 'pv-visually-hidden' -%}
    <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ variant.id }}" id="PEVariantId-{{ section.id }}">
    <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">
    {%- comment -%}
      The theme's ProductForm custom element looks up its own submit button
      with `this.querySelector('[type="submit"]')` — since every real
      "Ajouter au panier" button on this page lives outside this hidden
      form (linked via form="…"), that lookup would return null and throw
      before the cart request is ever sent. This dummy button keeps that
      lookup valid.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <button type="submit" name="add" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"></button>
    <div class="product-form__error-message alert alert--error" role="alert" hidden style="position:fixed;left:16px;right:16px;bottom:84px;z-index:70;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e11d48;color:#e11d48;padding:12px 16px;border-radius:12px;font-size:14px;"></div>
  {%- endform -%}
  <style>.pv-visually-hidden{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;padding:0;margin:-1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0,0,0,0);white-space:nowrap;border:0;}</style>

